<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Gaozu of Tang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">founded dynasty <a href="/years/618">618 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Li Yuan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Gaozu, born Li Yuan, was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a>. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a> general, he rebelled during the collapse of the Sui and founded the dynasty in 618 CE. He abdicated in favour of his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Li Shimin</a>, the future Emperor Taizong, after the Xuanwu Gate incident.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang.jpg" alt="Emperor Gaozu of Tang" width="204" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TangGaozu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the north the aristocrat <b>Li Yuan</b> rose and ascended the throne as Emperor Gaozu of Tang.</blockquote><a href="/empire/sui-dynasty">Sui Dynasty · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The Tang Dynasty was founded in 618 CE by <b>Li Yuan</b> (Emperor Gaozu), Duke of Tang and a Sui military commander at Taiyuan, who exploited the collapse of the Sui, brought down by Emperor Yang's disastrous campaigns against the Korean kingdom of Goguryeo (the Goguryeo–Sui War) and the…</blockquote><a href="/empire/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The ruling houses of the Northern Zhou, Sui and Tang came from a mixed Xianbei and Chinese aristocracy of the north-west: Empress Dugu, wife of the Sui founder, and the mother of the Tang founder <b>Li Yuan</b> were daughters of the Xianbei general Dugu Xin.</blockquote><a href="/empire/xianbei">Xianbei · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>After the fall of the Sui, <b>Li Yuan</b> took the throne at Chang'an as Emperor Gaozu.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/june-18">18 June in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Li Shimin, who had encouraged his father <b>Li Yuan</b>'s rebellion against the Sui, took the throne as the second Tang emperor, known after his death as Taizong.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/september-4">4 September in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The rebel Duke of Tang, <b>Li Yuan</b>, advancing on the Sui capital, routed an elite Sui army of 20,000 at Huoyi after an initial setback.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/september-8">8 September in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=34.31,108.86&amp;year=618" aria-label="Chang'an on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7319 921 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Emperor Gaozu of Tang"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7769 1191h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7769 1191h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=34.31,108.86&amp;year=618">What was here in 618 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
